"pull" runs "hg fetch", which is an optional extension.  When it is not enabled, hg prints an
error, which the program passes through after removing the "abort: " prefix.  The goal file
records the behavior when fetch is unavailable, which is the usual case; if the fetch extension is
enabled, this test fails and the goal file needs an update.

hg writes part of this message to standard output and part to standard error, and the program
merges the two streams with one thread apiece, so their relative order varies from run to run.
That is why this test case has a `sort-output` file.  Sorting is enough because the program writes
a whole line at a time, so no line is ever half from one stream and half from the other.
